Micro-purchase threshold means $10,000, except—
(1) For acquisitions of construction subject to the Davis-Bacon Act, $2,000;
(2) For acquisitions of services subject to the Service Contract Labor Standards statute, $2,500;
(3) $20,000 for acquisitions to support a contingency operation, humanitarian or peacekeeping operation, emergency or major disaster, or a crime of violence against a Federal employee.

Simplified acquisition threshold means $250,000, except in the case of a contingency operation or a humanitarian or peacekeeping operation it means $1,000,000.

Micro-purchase threshold and Simplified acquisition threshold — see 2.101 Definitions.

